---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const models = [
  { code: "D1", name: "Assign rider", q: "Which rider takes this order?", calm: "the nearest free rider" },
  { code: "D2", name: "Estimate time", q: "How long will it really take?", calm: "an honest ETA" },
  { code: "D3", name: "Next cook", q: "What should the kitchen start now?", calm: "the next dish in line" },
  { code: "D4", name: "Late risk", q: "Which order is about to slip?", calm: "the order that needs a nudge" },
  { code: "D5", name: "Zone check", q: "Is this inside the promise?", calm: "a safe yes or no" },
];
---
<Base title="Technology" description="The GoServe technology: a hyperlocal food OS with Jev, a decision engine that assigns riders, estimates time, and protects a 15-minute promise.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Technology</span>
      <h1 class="h1">A quiet engine doing loud work.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The magic of GoServe is not an animation or a gimmick. It is a decision
        engine, Jev, that answers the hard questions of a delivery in the same
        second you place an order. When Jev is unsure, it falls back to a safe
        rule. Nothing in the payment path depends on it. The food always moves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface" style="padding-block: var(--gs-space-8)">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: var(--gs-space-6)">Jev: five questions, every order.</h2>
      <div class="models">
        {
          models.map((m) => (
            <article class="model card">
              <div class="model-head">
                <span class="model-code">{m.code}</span>
                <h3 class="h3">{m.name}</h3>
              </div>
              <p class="model-q">{m.q}</p>
              <p class="model-calm"><strong>If unsure,</strong> {m.calm}.</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--gs-space-6)">
        Five more models (abuse and refund checks, offer choice, reorder nudges,
        support triage, copilot routing) follow in later phases.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container stack-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">The shape</span>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: var(--gs-space-4)">One product, many hands.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Customer, kitchen, rider, and ops share one codebase and one live feed.
          A single backend does the work, so everyone sees the same truth at the
          same time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="arch reveal">
        <li><strong>App</strong><span>One installable PWA. Customer, kitchen, rider, ops.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Backend</strong><span>Light, typed, and fast. Owns orders, money, and state.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Live feed</strong><span>Server-sent events. Status moves with no refresh.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Jev layer</strong><span>One wrapper. Model calls, thresholds, and safe fallbacks.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Automation</strong><span>Workflows for capture and alerts, so nothing is missed.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container container-narrow" style="text-align:center">
      <h2 class="h1" style="color:#fff">Built to be copied. Hard to catch.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="color:var(--gs-sage); margin-inline:auto">
        Anyone can buy a courier. Few can build an OS that thinks ahead.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/investors">Investor overview</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .models {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--gs-space-5);
  }
  .model-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--gs-space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--gs-space-3);
  }
  .model-code {
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--gs-ink-green);
    background: var(--gs-lime);
    border-radius: var(--gs-radius-s);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-size: var(--gs-text-sm);
  }
  .h3 {
    font-size: var(--gs-text-lg);
  }
  .model-q {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gs-ink-green);
  }
  .model-calm {
    font-size: var(--gs-text-sm);
    color: var(--gs-deep-green);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .stack-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.9fr;
    gap: var(--gs-space-8);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .arch {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gs-space-3);
  }
  .arch li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gs-lime);
    padding-left: var(--gs-space-4);
  }
  .arch strong {
    color: var(--gs-ink-green);
  }
  .arch span {
    font-size: var(--gs-text-sm);
    color: var(--gs-deep-green);
  }
  .cta {
    background: var(--gs-ink-green);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .stack-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
